  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Oceanographic and Fisheries Time-Series Data by T/S Oshoro-Maru",
  "description": "Hokkaido University has 5 sampling lines (155°E, 170°E, 175°30メE, 180°, 145°W longitude) in the North Pacific Ocean. The 180°-line is the longest time-series of the oceanographic and fisheries data collected by T/S Oshoro-Maru. Data includes zooplankton samples collected at stations between 37° and 51°N in the summers (mid-June) of 1979-2000 and hydrographic data (temperature, salinity and Secchi depth). The 180° time-series data sets have been published in the Data Record of Oceanographic Observation and Exploratory Fisheries Nos. 23-43 (Hokkaido University 1980-2000). [ Reference: PICES Scientific Report No. 18 2001, Proceedings of the PICES/CoML/IPRC Workshop on \"Impact of Climate Variability on Observation and Prediction of Ecosystem and Biodiversity Changes in the North Pacific\", http://www.pices.int/publications/scientific_reports/Report18/default.aspx. ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To observe the interannual variability and climate impacts in the North Pacific ecosystem.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23516110",
